course: dictionary
lesson: 10308
title: Towel: a word with two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a thing or an action. As a noun, a towel is a piece of thick soft cloth or paper used to dry your body, hands or dishes. «Bring a beach towel to the pool.» Here towel is a thing you can hold.
explain: Towel can also be a verb. To towel (off) means to dry yourself with a towel. «He towelled his hair after the swim.» The word did is the clue: he did something, so towelled is an action.
explain: Context tells you which towel is meant. A «tea towel» (UK) or «dish towel» (US) dries plates, and «paper towels» wipe up spills. Read the words around the word first, then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: A towel is a noun for a thing. To towel is a verb for an action.
fact: Towels are for drying your body, your hands or the dishes.
fact: Phrases with towel include «throw in the towel», which means give up, and «beach towel», «bath towel» and «hand towel».
fact: Good hygiene means using your own towel, drying your hands well after washing, because germs spread more on wet hands, and washing towels often.
fact: «A boy in Leeds put a towel over a heater to dry it; it started to burn and filled the room with smoke.» Never put a towel on a heater.
exercise: «Always use your own towel.» In this sentence, what kind of word is towel? | A verb, an action | An adjective, a describing word | *A noun, a thing you can hold | A verb, to dry
exercise: «He towelled his hair dry after the swim.» What does towelled mean? | Went swimming again | Cut very short | *Dried with a towel | Washed in the pool
exercise: Ella says «throw in the towel» means throw a towel at someone. What does it really mean? | *To give up | To swim very fast | To wash the dishes | To play a ball game
test: In the UK, what do you call a towel that dries dishes? | Beach towel | Hand towel | Bath towel | *Tea towel
test: Why should you dry your hands well after washing? | Wet hands look untidy | Hands get cold faster | *Germs spread more on wet hands | Water makes soap stronger
exam: «A boy in Leeds put a towel over a heater to dry it.» What happened next? | It turned into a blanket | It dried very fast and was fine | *It started to burn and filled the room with smoke | It was washed clean
